// cpu.node — PLACEHOLDER FILE
//
// This is NOT a real Node.js native addon. It is a placeholder committed to
// the repository so that the subpackage layout is complete and the loader
// (index.js) has a target to reference during local development.
//
// The actual prebuilt `cpu.node` binary is produced by CI (see
// .github/workflows) which compiles src/binding.cc against the modified
// llama.cpp sources and uploads the resulting .node as a build artifact.
// Before publishing `soulx-singer-dit-win32-x64-cpu` to npm, CI replaces
// this placeholder with the real compiled binary for win32-x64 (CPU build,
// no GPU acceleration).
//
// DO NOT require this file directly in production — it will fail to load as
// a native addon. Use the main `soulx-singer-dit` package, which selects and
// loads the appropriate prebuilt subpackage for your platform.
//
// Build target: win32-x64, CPU only (ggml backend).
